{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the matter was good in my eyes.</b> For I thought that you had no doubt concerning the word of the Blessed El — that you would conquer the land and that it was good — but rather that you wished to select the best portion of it for yourselves at present, in your saying, \">the cities we shall come to,\"> and this because you knew that you would not conquer it all in a single year, as it says: לֹא אֲגָרְשֶׁנּוּ מִפָּנֶיךָ בְּשָׁנָה אֶחָת (Exodus 23:29)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:07.216066766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}